       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Dose:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day under medical supervision. The usual OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg in one dose is double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks:** At this level the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events rises sharply, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n\n1. **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions)\n2. **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n3. **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** (for pain or fever)\n4. **1600 mg total per day**, for example 400 mg four times daily, if the 1600 was meant as the daily total\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first. Once you give me the corrected dose, I'll enter it right away."
